  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2504.11703",
  "abstract": "Progent is a novel security framework that enforces privilege control at the tool level for Large Language Model (LLM) agents. It restricts agents to making only necessary tool calls, blocking potentially malicious ones, and provides a domain-specific language for expressing fine-grained security policies. Progent's modular design allows for seamless integration with existing agent frameworks, requiring minimal code modifications, and supports flexible policy adjustments for rapid threat response.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "LLM agents face significant security risks due to over-privileged tool access. <strong>Progent</strong> addresses this by enforcing security at the tool level, restricting agents to necessary tool calls while blocking malicious ones. It features a domain-specific language for expressing fine-grained policies, flexible fallback actions, and dynamic policy updates.",
