    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "Progent's security policy language allows developers to define fine-grained controls over tool calls. Each policy specifies conditions for allowing or blocking tool calls based on their arguments. <strong>Policies</strong> can be assigned priorities and include fallback actions for handling blocked calls. Progent enforces these policies at runtime, intercepting tool calls and evaluating them against the defined policies.",
